Title: Fix parse-time wildcard fragility in armN_flat stamp prerequisites
Created: 2026-06-08
Author: HDMX-coding-agent

--- log ---
2026-06-08T09:49Z HDMX-coding-agent created

--- body ---
## Context

The four `armN_flat/.done` extraction stamps in `experiments/derived/score.mk`
(~207–239) take their prerequisites from `$(wildcard …/sota_exp3_armN_batch1/
run*/*.json)`. `$(wildcard)` expands at **parse time**, against the files
present when `make` reads the makefile — not when the rule runs. Two failure
modes follow:

1. **Fresh checkout / pre-acquire.** If the P1 raw replies are absent at parse
   time (clone before the acquire sweep, or after an archive move), the wildcard
   expands to the empty list. The stamp rule then has NO prerequisites: once
   `.done` exists it is considered up-to-date forever, so when the JSONs later
   land the extraction never re-runs. `armN_flat/` stays stale silently.
2. **New runs added.** Adding `run06/*.json` after a stamp exists does not mark
   the stamp out of date unless a *captured* prereq is newer — and a brand-new
   file was not in the parse-time set at all.

This is the deferred follow-up flagged in tickets 0460 and 0461 and in the
`feedback-make-stamp-discipline` memory. It is distinct from those: the stamps
themselves are the CORRECT idiom (dynamic multi-output, ~60 un-enumerable
files) — the bug is the *prerequisite source*, not the stamp.

## Scope note — the pattern is broader than armN

The same parse-time `$(wildcard)` feeds other score.mk prereqs:
- `ANALYSIS_EXP1_INPUT_CSVS := $(wildcard …/exp1_batch2/*.csv)` (prereq of the
  exp1_cross_eval.csv rule, 0460).
- `SCORE_OUTPUT_FILES := $(wildcard …)` (prereq of `measurements.jsonl`).
Decide whether to fix only the armN stamps (narrow) or address the class
(preferred, with one mechanism). Document the choice.

## Candidate fixes (executor decides; do not assume)

- **Depend on an acquire-produced sentinel.** P1 (`acquire.mk`) is the producer
  of `run*/*.json`; have the sweep write/`touch` a per-arm manifest
  (e.g. `sota_exp3_armN_batch1/.acquired`) and make the score stamp depend on
  THAT stable path (no wildcard). Cleanest across the acquire→score seam, and
  consistent with the phase-boundary discipline (test_score_build_no_acquire).
- **Recursively-expanded prereq via a shell `find`** in a `$(shell …)` guarded
  to run at build time, or a `.SECONDEXPANSION` prereq — re-globs later but
  still mtime-based; partial.
- **Order-only + always-extract when explicitly invoked** — simplest, loses
  incremental skip; acceptable only if extraction is cheap.
Evaluate against: correctness on fresh checkout, no money-gated acquire
triggered by a P2 dry-run (the score/acquire seam invariant), incremental skip
preserved.

## Relevant files

- `experiments/derived/score.mk` (~183 EXP1 csvs, ~207–239 armN stamps, the
  SCORE_OUTPUT_FILES wildcard).
- `experiments/acquire.mk` — if the sentinel-manifest fix is chosen, the sweep
  writes it here (P1 side).
- `tests/test_score_build_no_acquire.py` — keep its invariant intact.

## Test (write first — red)

`tests/test_armN_stamp_rebuilds_on_new_data.py` (integration — uses tmp tree +
subprocess `make`): create an EMPTY arm input dir, build the stamp (succeeds
with empty input), then drop a `run01/*.json` in and re-run make; assert the
stamp rule re-fires (extraction re-runs). Against today's wildcard rule this is
RED (stamp stays up-to-date); the fix makes it GREEN. Mark `@pytest.mark.integration`.

## Verification

- [ ] Reproduction test red on current code, green after the fix.
- [ ] Fresh-checkout simulation: empty input dir → stamp → add data → stamp
      rebuilds.
- [ ] A P2 dry-run (`make -n -f score.mk all-outcomes`) still triggers NO
      acquire/LLM step (test_score_build_no_acquire stays green).
- [ ] `make check` green.

## Invariants

- The stamp idiom for armN stays (do not "flatten" to plain rules — outputs are
  dynamic/multi-file).
- No P2 target may (re)acquire raw replies (score/acquire seam).
- exp1_cross_eval.csv (0460) and measurements.jsonl rebuild behavior unchanged
  unless the class fix is deliberately extended to them.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] armN extraction re-runs when its raw inputs appear or change after parse
      time (no silent stale `armN_flat/`).
- [ ] Reproduction test guards the regression.
- [ ] score/acquire seam invariant preserved; `make check` green.

